{"metadata":{"title":"Origami to SwiftUI reference","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each Origami patch becomes in SwiftUI, so you know which construct — or which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" helper — to reach for."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI both describe how values flow and change over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time, so the translations map onto SwiftUI’s own tools: computed properties for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pure math, gestures and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" for interaction, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" for motion. Most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patches land on a native SwiftUI construct. A few need a helper from the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library, named after the patch it stands in for.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Patch → SwiftUI","anchor":"Patch-%E2%86%92-SwiftUI"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami patch"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patch (Add, interpolate, logic)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression (native)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/interaction(down:position:onTap:onDoubleTap:onLongPress:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"text":" — Drag","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Magnification \/ Pinch","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MagnifyGesture","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (native)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.PopSwitch"},{"type":"text","text":" — Pop Switch"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" flipped on a threshold, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".spring"},{"type":"text","text":" pop (native)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"builtin.layer.shape"},{"text":" — Shape (triangle)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/RoundedTriangle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State \/ memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" + update logic (native)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop \/ Spring)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(.spring)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (native)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"How the categories map","anchor":"How-the-categories-map"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patches"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", interpolation, logic — carry no state. They run an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input through math and emit a result, which is exactly a computed property or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inline expression."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" exposes discrete outputs: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each becomes a SwiftUI gesture whose result lands in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"code":".interaction(…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier attaches only the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recognizers you ask for, so gesture arbitration stays clean.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State and memory","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Switch"},{"text":" — remember a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between evaluations. That is what ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" is for; the update path is a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"text":" — drives a value toward a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"target over time, which is a state change wrapped in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"text":" modifier.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One naming note: Origami’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"interpolation"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (mapping one range"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"onto another), not SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier for view insertion and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"removal."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"When-a-mapping-isnt-exact","text":"When a mapping isn’t exact","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics have no direct SwiftUI equivalent — continuous-time springs,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"custom JavaScript patches, absolute-position layout. Rather than approximate them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"silently, each translated view marks the gap with an inline ","type":"text"},{"code":"TODO","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in its source,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the caveat travels with the code. The individual pattern pages link to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"source where those notes live.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/RoundedTriangle":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An upward-pointing triangle with uniformly rounded corners."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RoundedTriangle"}],"title":"RoundedTriangle","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RoundedTriangle"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/roundedtriangle","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/RoundedTriangle","role":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swami","title":"Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami patterns, rebuilt as SwiftUI you can read — each one a worked example of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patches behind it, so you can see how a prototype’s behavior is written and reach for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same patch on your own layers."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}